2. Adapted third-party work
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The OPS theme visuals and interaction design of opencode-dash.html are adapted
from the following project:

- agent-display - MIT License - Copyright (c) cyberdaddyleo -
  https://github.com/cyberdaddyleo/agent-display

The adaptation keeps the original copyright and license notice, as required by
the MIT License, and the relationship is stated in the README credits and in the
attribution line rendered in the page footer.

What was adapted: the OPS paper-engineering theme - the dispatch flywheel, the
rotating band with data blocks, the convergence nodes, the four bottom panels
and the paper / fluorescent colour scheme.

What was rewritten: the entire data layer. The original page drives everything
from an in-page simulator that generates sample metrics; this project replaces
it with a local read-only bridge that reads live activity from a running
OpenCode instance (sessions, tool calls, steps, token usage and cost). The
bridge, the single-file page, the launcher and the documentation in this
repository are original work.

No code, data or asset is copied verbatim from the upstream project beyond the
visual and interaction design described above.

